          "citation": "2026 IL App (1st) 251913",
          "court": "Appellate Court of Illinois",
          "year": 2026,
          "date_decided": "2026-08-26",
          "holding": "The court reversed an order closing the case to private guardianship with the paternal grandmother, holding the best-interests finding was against the manifest weight of the evidence where the mother had complied with services and every caseworker recommended return home.",
          "relevance": "Guardianship is not a substitute for return home absent evidence that reunification efforts have failed.",
          "quote": "The circuit court's finding that this was in K.W.'s best interest was against the manifest weight of the evidence.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/10958450/in-re-kw/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 10958450
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Troxel v. Granville",
          "citation": "530 U.S. 57 (2000)",
          "court": "Supreme Court of the United States",
          "year": 2000,
          "date_decided": "2000-06-05",
          "holding": "The Court affirmed invalidation of a grandparent visitation order, holding that Washington's statute as applied violated the mother's due process right to direct her children's upbringing because the trial court gave no special weight to a fit parent's own determination.",
          "relevance": "The federal constitutional baseline In re R.L.S. operates against: a fit parent's decision must receive special weight over a non-parent's competing custody or visitation claim.",
          "quote": "That aspect of the case is important, for there is a presumption that fit parents act in the best interests of their children.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/1087668/troxel-v-granville/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 1087668
        }
